// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// DATABASE SCHEMA — PLACEHOLDER / MARKER ONLY (NOT WIRED UP)
//
// This file is intentionally named `.placeholder` so no ORM tooling picks it
// up. It documents the future data needs for the members-only performance-
// tracking feature. No database, Prisma, or other ORM is installed yet.
//
// When performance tracking is built, decide on a database + ORM (Prisma,
// Drizzle, Supabase, etc.), rename/replace this with a real schema, and add
// the corresponding packages. The auth provider (see middleware.ts) should be
// chosen first so user identity maps cleanly to AthleteProfile.
//
// Sketch of the eventual models (illustrative — not final):
//
//   AthleteProfile
//     id, userId (from auth provider), firstName, lastName, birthDate,
//     primaryPosition, throws, bats, createdAt
//
//   TrainingSession
//     id, athleteId -> AthleteProfile, date, type (coaching|performance),
//     coachId, notes
//
//   Metric  (time-series performance data — the core of "progress over time")
//     id, athleteId -> AthleteProfile, sessionId -> TrainingSession,
//     kind (exitVelocity | launchAngle | sixtyYardDash | benchPress | ...),
//     value, unit, recordedAt
//
// The Metric table is deliberately generic (kind/value/unit) so new tracked
// stats can be added without schema migrations.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
